1802	 * read snapshot, so a concurrent writer committing between two statements is
1803	 * visible to the later one but not the earlier one. Projections cross-checked
1804	 * against history then disagree, and a fail-closed reader reports that torn read
1805	 * as `STATE_CORRUPTED` even though nothing on disk is inconsistent. WAL keeps a
1806	 * deferred read transaction from blocking writers.
